      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a strong oversimplification to claim that \"free trade is always better,\" as real-world economic policy is nuanced and context-dependent.\n\nHowever, the *strong bias* in the \"mainstream view\" is that unconstrained protectionism fundamentally distorts the highly efficient global division of labor that free trade supports.\n\nThe consensus leans toward advocating for **smarter trade policy** that might selectively support essential national security needs, rather than the **absolute and broad use of protectionism** to shield all domestic interests at the cost of overall global efficiency.",
